    "text": "<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0109_8e967f3a9b29.png\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 206px; height: 184px;\" /><br /><br /><math><mrow>&#160;<mi>&#964;</mi> <mo>=</mo> <mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">P</mtext> <mo>&#215;</mo> <mtext>E</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">P</mtext> <mtext>E</mtext> <mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace> <mtext>sin</mtext> <mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#952;</mi> <mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace> <mtext>.... (i)</mtext> </mrow> </math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>E</mi><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi><mi>&#945;</mi></math><br /><br />[&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi></math> is the moment of inertia and &alpha; the angular acceleration]<br /><br />Since displacement is small sin <math> <mrow> <mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#952;</mi> <mover> <mo>=</mo> <mo>&#8764;</mo> </mover> <mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#952;</mi> </mrow> </math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi>I</mi><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>-</mi><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">PE</mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#952;</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mtext>&#945;</mtext><mo>=</mo><mi>-</mi><mfrac><mtext>PE</mtext><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">I</mtext></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#952;</mi></math><br /><br />The angular frequency of oscillation is given by<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#969;</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">PE</mtext><mi>I</mi></mfrac></msqrt></math><br /><br />The potential energy is lowest when the dipole moment is aligned with the field and highest when the two are antialigned."
